IMPORT prelude

-- Administration Act 1903 (Western Australia) -- who takes on intestacy (s 14 and its Table, s 15 de facto partners, s 12A
-- children of unmarried parents, s 13(1a) land held as tenants in common), which grant a death calls for (ss 6, 7, 25, 33,
-- 36), the small-estate route to the Principal Registrar (s 55), bank deposits paid without a grant (s 139), and when a will
-- may be put in evidence (s 71).
--
-- Edition: compilation incorporating amendments to the Administration Amendment Act 2022 (No. 5 of 2022, in operation
-- 30 March 2022), whose notes list the Administration (Intestacy Legacy Amounts) Orders 2023 and 2025 by name only, as
-- deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/mrdoc_49096.txt (retrieved 7 September 2026). The deposit states no
-- compilation number; the last reprint it lists is Reprint 12, as at 15 April 2016. An uncommenced amendment (Assisted
-- Reproductive Technology and Surrogacy Act 2025 Pt. 17 Div. 1, to be proclaimed) is listed but its text is not in the deposit.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement au/wa:REQ-0002 (subjects/au/wa/requirements.jsonl), priority 1, raised 10 times by the three
-- Western Australian cradle-to-grave lives: chloe c087, c088, c096, c098; jake k084, k088, k098; daniel d074, d086, d093.
-- They ask: which grant follows a death with a will and an executor; who takes when Sue dies intestate leaving two children
-- (c088, k088: "half each"); who takes when Jake dies divorced and intestate leaving one child, Ruby (k098), whether there
-- must be a grant and whether the Public Trustee may act; whether Jake takes anything under a will that leaves everything to
-- his mother (k084). SCOPED to those questions and the definitions, conditions and exceptions needed to answer them: the
-- whole s 14 Table (all eleven items, since the item turns on who survives), s 15, s 12A, s 13(1a), ss 6, 7, 25, 33, 36,
-- 55, 139 and 71.
--
-- Not encoded: the Fourth Schedule (the surviving spouse's election to take the home), s 14(5) income, s 14(7) partition,
-- insolvent estates (s 10A, Fifth Schedule), sureties, revocation, special and limited grants (ss 26-42), accounts (ss 43-
-- 47A), resealing of foreign grants (Part III), caveats (Part IV), infants' shares (ss 17, 17A), and the Family Provision Act
-- 1972 claims that s 60A preserves. Survivorship between joint tenants, the validity of a will, superannuation death benefits
-- and the Public Trustee's own powers are in other Acts and are not here. Interest under s 14(4) is encoded as simple
-- interest on whole years only.
--
-- AMOUNTS AS INPUTS. The Table's sums ($472 000, $705 000, $56 500) are the "original sums" the Act states (s 14A(1)); a
-- Minister's order under s 14A(2) may declare others, and the 2023 and 2025 Orders are named in the deposit's notes without
-- their figures. So every function takes the sums as an input (`Sums`); `the original sums` is what the Act states. The s 139
-- bank-deposit ceiling is likewise an input: the section says "$1 200, or such other amount as may for the time being be
-- declared by proclamation", and the deposit's note 4 says it "is now declared to be $50 000".
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules conventions (the skill was not available in this
-- session; the finished naive encodings in subjects/sg were followed). No pipeline, no coverage table, no independent test
-- pass, no human gate. NOT for public use. See NOTES.md.

§ `Administration Act 1903 -- intestacy and grants`

§§ `s 14(1A), 14A(1) -- the sums in the Table`

-- s 14A(1): "original sum, for a specified item, means -- (a) in the case of item 2 -- $472 000; (b) in the case of item
-- 3(a) and (b) -- $705 000; (c) in the case of item 3(b)(i) -- $56 500; (d) in the case of item 6 -- $56 500".
-- s 14(1B): the declared sum that applies is the one "under the order that has effect at the time the intestate dies".
DECLARE Sums HAS
    `item 2 sum` IS A NUMBER
    `item 3 sum` IS A NUMBER
    `item 3(b)(i) sum` IS A NUMBER
    `item 6 sum` IS A NUMBER

`the original sums` MEANS Sums WITH
    `item 2 sum` IS 472000
    `item 3 sum` IS 705000
    `item 3(b)(i) sum` IS 56500
    `item 6 sum` IS 56500

§§ `s 15 -- de facto partners`

-- s 15(1): no husband or wife, and a de facto partner who lived with the intestate "for a period of at least 2 years
-- immediately before the death" takes what a husband or wife would have taken.
-- s 15(2): a husband or wife AND such a de facto partner, where the intestate "did not, during the whole or any part of that
-- period, live as the husband or wife of the person to whom he or she was married": the de facto partner takes "one-half of
-- the intestate property to which the husband or wife would have been entitled" and the spouse the other half.
-- s 15(3): the same, but at least 5 years: the de facto partner takes it all.
-- s 15(5): an entitled de facto partner "is to be taken to be a husband or wife" for s 14.
DECLARE Family HAS
    `leaves a husband or wife` IS A BOOLEAN
    `years lived as de facto partners immediately before death` IS A NUMBER
    `lived as husband or wife of the spouse during that period` IS A BOOLEAN
    `children who survived` IS A NUMBER
    `children who died leaving issue who survived` IS A NUMBER
    `parents who survived` IS A NUMBER
    `leaves a brother or sister or child of one` IS A BOOLEAN
    `grandparents who survived` IS A NUMBER
    `leaves an uncle or aunt or child of one` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the family` IS A Family
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a de facto partner is entitled` IF
    `the family`'s `years lived as de facto partners immediately before death` AT LEAST 2
    AND (    (NOT `the family`'s `leaves a husband or wife`)
          OR (NOT `the family`'s `lived as husband or wife of the spouse during that period`))

GIVEN `the family` IS A Family
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the de facto partner's fraction` MEANS
    IF NOT `a de facto partner is entitled` `the family` THEN 0
    ELSE IF NOT `the family`'s `leaves a husband or wife` THEN 1
         ELSE IF `the family`'s `years lived as de facto partners immediately before death` AT LEAST 5 THEN 1
              ELSE 1 DIVIDED BY 2

GIVEN `the family` IS A Family
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the husband's or wife's fraction` MEANS
    IF `the family`'s `leaves a husband or wife` THEN 1 MINUS `the de facto partner's fraction` `the family` ELSE 0

GIVEN `the family` IS A Family
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `leaves a partner for the Table` IF
    `the family`'s `leaves a husband or wife` OR `a de facto partner is entitled` `the family`

§§ `s 14(1) Table -- which item applies`

-- Items: 1 a husband or wife takes "all household chattels"; 2 husband or wife and issue; 3 husband or wife and "a parent, a
-- brother or sister, or child of a brother or sister, but leaving no issue"; 4 husband or wife only; 5 "issue but no husband
-- or wife"; 6 parent(s) and brother, sister or child of one; 7 parent(s) only; 8 brothers, sisters or their children only;
-- 9 grandparents; 10 uncles, aunts or their children; 11 none of these: "the whole of the intestate property passes to the
-- Crown by way of escheat". Item 1 runs alongside items 2 to 4; this function returns the item that divides the rest.
GIVEN `the family` IS A Family
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the number of lines of issue` MEANS
    `the family`'s `children who survived` PLUS `the family`'s `children who died leaving issue who survived`

GIVEN `the family` IS A Family
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the Table item` MEANS
    IF `leaves a partner for the Table` `the family`
    THEN IF `the number of lines of issue` `the family` GREATER THAN 0 THEN 2
         ELSE IF `the family`'s `parents who survived` GREATER THAN 0 OR `the family`'s `leaves a brother or sister or child of one` THEN 3
              ELSE 4
    ELSE IF `the number of lines of issue` `the family` GREATER THAN 0 THEN 5
         ELSE IF `the family`'s `parents who survived` GREATER THAN 0 AND `the family`'s `leaves a brother or sister or child of one` THEN 6
              ELSE IF `the family`'s `parents who survived` GREATER THAN 0 THEN 7
                   ELSE IF `the family`'s `leaves a brother or sister or child of one` THEN 8
                        ELSE IF `the family`'s `grandparents who survived` GREATER THAN 0 THEN 9
                             ELSE IF `the family`'s `leaves an uncle or aunt or child of one` THEN 10
                                  ELSE 11

GIVEN `the family` IS A Family
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the property passes to the Crown` IF
    `the Table item` `the family` EQUALS 11

§§ `s 14(1) Table items 2 to 4, s 14(3) -- the partner's share`

-- Item 2(a): where the net value (other than household chattels) "does not exceed the sum of $472 000" the husband or wife
-- takes the whole. (b): above it, the husband or wife takes $472 000 "absolutely, together with interest" and "of the
-- residue ... one third and the issue ... the other two-thirds".
-- s 14(3): with "a husband or wife and one child; or ... the issue of one child", read "one-half" and "half".
-- Item 3(a): not exceeding $705 000, the whole; (b): above it, $705 000 and "of the residue ... one-half".
-- Item 4: "the whole of the intestate property".
-- s 14(2)(b): "the net value of the intestate property is the net value of that property at the date of the death".
-- `net value` below is the net value OTHER THAN household chattels.
GIVEN `the family` IS A Family, `the sums` IS A Sums, `net value` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the partner's share` MEANS
    IF `the Table item` `the family` EQUALS 2
    THEN IF `net value` AT MOST `the sums`'s `item 2 sum` THEN `net value`
         ELSE IF `the number of lines of issue` `the family` EQUALS 1
              THEN `the sums`'s `item 2 sum` PLUS ((`net value` MINUS `the sums`'s `item 2 sum`) DIVIDED BY 2)
              ELSE `the sums`'s `item 2 sum` PLUS ((`net value` MINUS `the sums`'s `item 2 sum`) DIVIDED BY 3)
    ELSE IF `the Table item` `the family` EQUALS 3
         THEN IF `net value` AT MOST `the sums`'s `item 3 sum` THEN `net value`
              ELSE `the sums`'s `item 3 sum` PLUS ((`net value` MINUS `the sums`'s `item 3 sum`) DIVIDED BY 2)
         ELSE IF `the Table item` `the family` EQUALS 4 THEN `net value`
              ELSE 0

-- s 15(2): where a husband or wife and a de facto partner share, each takes half of this.
GIVEN `the family` IS A Family, `the sums` IS A Sums, `net value` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the husband's or wife's share` MEANS
    `the partner's share` `the family` `the sums` `net value` TIMES `the husband's or wife's fraction` `the family`

GIVEN `the family` IS A Family, `the sums` IS A Sums, `net value` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the de facto partner's share` MEANS
    `the partner's share` `the family` `the sums` `net value` TIMES `the de facto partner's fraction` `the family`

-- s 14(4): the husband or wife entitled to the item 2 or item 3 sum is also entitled to "5% per annum on the sum ... calculated
-- from the date of death of the intestate to the date of the payment of that sum". Whole years only here.
GIVEN `sum` IS A NUMBER, `years unpaid` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the statutory interest` MEANS
    `sum` TIMES 5 DIVIDED BY 100 TIMES `years unpaid`

§§ `s 14(1) Table items 2 and 5, s 14(2b) -- the issue`

-- Item 5: "dies leaving issue but no husband or wife -- the issue shall be entitled in accordance with subsection (2b) to the
-- whole of the intestate property".
-- s 14(2b)(a): "where a person is the only entitled issue of the intestate, then that person is entitled to all".
-- s 14(2b)(b): otherwise the property is "divided into as many equal parts as there are children of the intestate who -- (i)
-- survived the intestate; or (ii) left issue who survived the intestate"; (c) a dead child's part goes to that child's issue.
GIVEN `the family` IS A Family, `the sums` IS A Sums, `net value` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the issue's share` MEANS
    IF `the Table item` `the family` EQUALS 2 THEN `net value` MINUS `the partner's share` `the family` `the sums` `net value`
    ELSE IF `the Table item` `the family` EQUALS 5 THEN `net value`
         ELSE 0

GIVEN `the family` IS A Family, `the sums` IS A Sums, `net value` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`each child's part` MEANS
    IF `the number of lines of issue` `the family` EQUALS 0 THEN 0
    ELSE `the issue's share` `the family` `the sums` `net value` DIVIDED BY `the number of lines of issue` `the family`

§§ `s 14(1) Table items 3, 6, 7, 8 -- parents, brothers and sisters`

-- Item 3(b) "as to the other half": (i)(A) if "that other half does not exceed the sum of $56 500 ... or if no brother, sister,
-- or child of a brother or sister survives" the parents take it; (B) otherwise the parents take $56 500 and "of the remainder
-- ... one-half", the brothers and sisters and children of deceased ones the other half; (ii) no parent: the brothers and
-- sisters take the other half.
-- Item 6(a): not exceeding $56 500, the parents take the whole; (b): above it, $56 500 and "of the residue ... one half", the
-- brothers and sisters the other half. Item 7: the parents take the whole. Item 8: the brothers and sisters take the whole.
GIVEN `the family` IS A Family, `the sums` IS A Sums, `net value` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the other half under item 3` MEANS
    IF `net value` AT MOST `the sums`'s `item 3 sum` THEN 0
    ELSE (`net value` MINUS `the sums`'s `item 3 sum`) DIVIDED BY 2

GIVEN `the family` IS A Family, `the sums` IS A Sums, `net value` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the parents' share` MEANS
    IF `the family`'s `parents who survived` EQUALS 0 THEN 0
    ELSE IF `the Table item` `the family` EQUALS 3
         THEN IF `the other half under item 3` `the family` `the sums` `net value` AT MOST `the sums`'s `item 3(b)(i) sum`
                 OR (NOT `the family`'s `leaves a brother or sister or child of one`)
              THEN `the other half under item 3` `the family` `the sums` `net value`
              ELSE `the sums`'s `item 3(b)(i) sum`
                   PLUS ((`the other half under item 3` `the family` `the sums` `net value` MINUS `the sums`'s `item 3(b)(i) sum`) DIVIDED BY 2)
         ELSE IF `the Table item` `the family` EQUALS 6
              THEN IF `net value` AT MOST `the sums`'s `item 6 sum` THEN `net value`
                   ELSE `the sums`'s `item 6 sum` PLUS ((`net value` MINUS `the sums`'s `item 6 sum`) DIVIDED BY 2)
              ELSE IF `the Table item` `the family` EQUALS 7 THEN `net value`
                   ELSE 0

GIVEN `the family` IS A Family, `the sums` IS A Sums, `net value` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the brothers' and sisters' share` MEANS
    IF `the Table item` `the family` EQUALS 3
    THEN `the other half under item 3` `the family` `the sums` `net value` MINUS `the parents' share` `the family` `the sums` `net value`
    ELSE IF `the Table item` `the family` EQUALS 6 THEN `net value` MINUS `the parents' share` `the family` `the sums` `net value`
         ELSE IF `the Table item` `the family` EQUALS 8 THEN `net value`
              ELSE 0

§§ `s 14(1) -- only the intestate property`

-- s 14(1): the Table distributes "the property as to which they die intestate (in this section called the intestate
-- property)". A will that disposes of everything leaves nothing for the Table.
GIVEN `net estate` IS A NUMBER, `value disposed of by the will` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the intestate property` MEANS
    IF `value disposed of by the will` AT LEAST `net estate` THEN 0 ELSE `net estate` MINUS `value disposed of by the will`

§§ `s 12A -- children of parents not married to each other`

-- s 12A(1): "the relationship between a child and his parents shall be determined irrespective of whether the parents are or
-- have been married to each other". s 12A(2)(b): where they are not or have not been married, the relationship is recognised
-- only "(i) if parentage is admitted by or established against the parent in his lifetime; and (ii) where the purpose ...
-- enures for the benefit of the parent, if parentage has been so admitted or established in the lifetime of the child".
-- s 12A(2a): (2)(b) does not apply to a relationship established by the Artificial Conception Act 1985.
GIVEN `parents are or have been married to each other` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `established by the Artificial Conception Act` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `parentage admitted or established in the parent's lifetime` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the purpose enures for the benefit of the parent` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `parentage admitted or established in the child's lifetime` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the relationship is recognised` IF
    `parents are or have been married to each other`
    OR `established by the Artificial Conception Act`
    OR (    `parentage admitted or established in the parent's lifetime`
        AND (    (NOT `the purpose enures for the benefit of the parent`)
              OR `parentage admitted or established in the child's lifetime`))

§§ `s 13(1a) -- land held for two or more`

-- s 13(1a): "When, pursuant to subsection (1), real estate is held on trust for 2 or more persons, it shall be held as if it had
-- been devised to those persons as tenants in common."
GIVEN `persons entitled` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the land is held as for tenants in common` IF
    `persons entitled` AT LEAST 2

§§ `ss 6, 7, 25, 33, 36 -- which grant`

-- s 6: the Court may "grant probate of the will or administration of the estate of any deceased person leaving property ... in
-- Western Australia". s 7: "probate to one or more of the executors named in any will".
-- s 33(1): "Where an infant is sole executor, administration with the will annexed may be granted to the guardian ... until
-- such infant has attained the age of 18 years".
-- s 36: "Where a person dies leaving a will but without having appointed an executor, or leaving a will and having appointed an
-- executor who is not willing and competent to take probate or is resident out of Western Australia, the Court may appoint an
-- administrator". s 25: administration "of the estate of a person dying intestate".
-- The encoder's reading: s 36 is a power ("may"), so an executor resident outside WA points to administration with the will
-- annexed only as the Court's option; this function names the grant the Act points to, not the Court's decision.
DECLARE Grant IS ONE OF
    `probate`
    `administration with the will annexed`
    `letters of administration`

DECLARE Death HAS
    `left a will` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the will appoints an executor` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the executor is an infant` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the executor is willing and competent` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the executor resides in Western Australia` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the death` IS A Death
GIVETH A Grant
`the grant the Act points to` MEANS
    IF NOT `the death`'s `left a will` THEN `letters of administration`
    ELSE IF NOT `the death`'s `the will appoints an executor` THEN `administration with the will annexed`
         ELSE IF `the death`'s `the executor is an infant` THEN `administration with the will annexed`
              ELSE IF `the death`'s `the executor is willing and competent` AND `the death`'s `the executor resides in Western Australia`
                   THEN `probate`
                   ELSE `administration with the will annexed`

§§ `s 25 -- who may be granted administration on intestacy`

-- s 25(1): the Court may grant administration "to the following persons (separately or conjointly) being of the full age of 18
-- years ... (a) one or more of the persons entitled in distribution to the estate of the intestate; (b) any other person, whether
-- a creditor or not, if there be no such person entitled as aforesaid resident within the jurisdiction and fit to be so
-- entrusted, or if the person entitled as aforesaid fails, when duly cited, to appear and apply for administration".
-- s 3: "administrator includes the Public Trustee". The Public Trustee Act 1941 (not encoded) is a separate route.
GIVEN `age` IS A NUMBER,
      `is entitled in distribution` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `an entitled person is resident and fit` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the entitled person failed when cited` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may be granted administration` IF
    `age` AT LEAST 18
    AND (    `is entitled in distribution`
          OR (NOT `an entitled person is resident and fit`)
          OR `the entitled person failed when cited`)

-- The same test for "any other person" that is not a natural person (the Public Trustee); the age words are not applied.
GIVEN `an entitled person is resident and fit` IS A BOOLEAN, `the entitled person failed when cited` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Public Trustee may be granted administration under s 25(1)(b)` IF
    (NOT `an entitled person is resident and fit`) OR `the entitled person failed when cited`

§§ `s 55 -- small estates`

-- s 55: "In all cases where a person dies leaving property not exceeding $10 000 in value, application for probate or
-- administration may be made direct to the Principal Registrar or to a district agent".
GIVEN `value of the property` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may apply direct to the Principal Registrar` IF
    `value of the property` AT MOST 10000

§§ `s 139 -- bank deposits paid without a grant`

-- s 139(1): a sum "not exceeding the amount of $1 200, or such other amount as may for the time being be declared by
-- proclamation" standing to the deceased's credit in an ADI, "if no probate or administration is produced to that ADI within
-- one month of the death ... and no notice in writing of any will and of intention to prove it or of an intention to apply for
-- administration is given to the ADI within that period", the ADI "may apply" to funeral expenses and the balance to "the
-- widower, widow, parent or child of the deceased person or a person who was living as a de facto partner of the deceased
-- person immediately before the deceased person's death". The ceiling is an input (note 4 of the deposit: now $50 000).
GIVEN `balance` IS A NUMBER,
      `the ceiling` IS A NUMBER,
      `a month has passed since the death` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `a grant was produced within the month` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `notice was given within the month` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the ADI may pay without a grant` IF
    `balance` AT MOST `the ceiling`
    AND `a month has passed since the death`
    AND (NOT `a grant was produced within the month`)
    AND (NOT `notice was given within the month`)

DECLARE Relation IS ONE OF
    `widower or widow`
    `parent`
    `child`
    `de facto partner immediately before death`
    `brother or sister`
    `other`

GIVEN `the relation` IS A Relation
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may receive the balance under s 139(1)(a)` IF
    CONSIDER `the relation`
    WHEN `widower or widow` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `parent` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `child` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `de facto partner immediately before death` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `s 71 -- a will in evidence before probate`

-- s 71: "No will or codicil of any deceased person shall be registered or receivable or admissible in evidence, except in
-- criminal proceedings, or upon application for probate or letters of administration, or in proceedings relating to the
-- validity of any such will or codicil, or in proceedings under this Part, until probate or letters of administration in
-- respect of the estate comprised therein shall have been issued or obtained."
DECLARE Proceeding IS ONE OF
    `criminal proceedings`
    `an application for a grant`
    `proceedings on the validity of the will`
    `any other proceedings`

GIVEN `the proceeding` IS A Proceeding, `a grant has issued` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the will is admissible in evidence` IF
    `a grant has issued`
    OR (CONSIDER `the proceeding`
        WHEN `any other proceedings` THEN FALSE
        OTHERWISE TRUE)
